# Git Rules

## Commit message trailers

The last three lines of every commit message must be, in this exact order:

```
Assisted-By: <model name>
Signed-off-by: <author from git-identity rule>
Change-Id: <generated or preserved Change-Id>
```

- Use the author name and email defined in the `git-identity.mdc` rule for the `Signed-off-by` line.
- Update the model name if the underlying model changes. Use the model name without the company name (e.g. `Claude Opus 4.6`, not `Anthropic Claude Opus 4.6`).
- If amending an existing commit, preserve its original `Change-Id`.
- NEVER add a `Co-authored-by` tag.
